{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c571","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07310-6156-7c60-80e0-f470e765d1c6"},"sequence":275,"recorded_at":1780531400000545,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"140ff5d5-e18a-408c-95de-5cdece639198"},"task_id":"140ff5d5-e18a-408c-95de-5cdece639198","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"140ff5d5-e18a-408c-95de-5cdece639198","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/prior-merge-report.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32jeti — base-refresh merge report (rev 7 → republish)\n2|\n3|Run: RUN-260905-ea9a88 ([implementer] developer (muse)).\n4|Brief: `integration_base_moved` refused rev 7 — trunk advanced to `2512f20`\n5|(sibling STORY-260830-3m2mw8 landed) with changes to `LOGBOOK.md` and\n6|`README.md`, which this Change Request also changes. Refresh onto trunk,\n7|resolve the overlap in those two files, republish. Change no Go file.\n8|\n9|## Pre-merge identity (read-only verification)\n10|\n11|- Story branch tip `8fbc052`, fork base `57afcc6`, trunk `2512f20`\n12|  (`git merge-base HEAD 2512f20` = `57afcc6`).\n13|- Rev-7 patch file set (60 paths incl. 2 untracked) is identical to the\n14|  worktree diff-vs-base file set: the tree IS the accepted rev-7 content.\n15|- Trunk gained since fork: LOGBOOK +86, README +29/−6. This story adds:\n16|  LOGBOOK +137, README +138/−4. Only these two files overlap. No other\n17|  path is touched by both sides.\n18|\n19|## LOGBOOK.md — merged, both sides kept whole (894 lines = 675 + 137 + 86 − 4)\n20|\n21|The 4-line deficit from the naive sum is the two `## 2026-09-05` /\n22|`## 2026-09-04` date headers plus their blanks, which are byte-identical\n23|on both sides and counted once. Zero lines removed from either side\n24|(`diff` both directions: additions only).\n25|\n26|- `## 2026-09-05`: our 0935/0926/0830/0510/0435/0429/0327, then sibling 0022\n27|  (00:22 is older than all seven; newest-first preserved).\n28|- `## 2026-09-04`: sibling 2340/2210/2147 (21:xx–23:xx), then our\n29|  0230/0210/0115 (00:xx–02:xx); newest-first preserved.\n30|- Tail after base `### 2113` (EOF appendix, arrival order): sibling 5\n31|  TASK-entries (landed first), then our 2321/1244. Sibling relative order\n32|  untouched; no sibling entry dropped, rewritten, or reordered.\n33|- Byte-identity asserted in-script: sibling 0022 block (10 lines), 09-04\n34|  block (26 lines), tail block (43 lines) equal trunk bytes; our blocks\n35|  equal pre-merge worktree bytes. Script: `/tmp/splice_logbook.py`.\n36|\n37|## README.md — merged onto trunk text, contradictions resolved (not concatenated)\n38|\n39|1. Our `## Provider Plugin Discovery and Trust` + `## Provider Plugin JSONL\n40|   Protocol` sections inserted before `## Canonical JSON …` (region trunk\n41|   does not touch). Sibling conpty / 15.3#3 / single-clause paragraphs kept.\n42|2. Refusal-arm inventories (the brief's explicit check): the document now\n43|   describes THREE per-package inventories — provider (\"from its own\n44|   source\"), provhost (\"from its own source\"), terminalbackend\n45|   (\"AST-derived …\"). Added one plain sentence to the provhost section:\n46|   the three are independent implementations sharing no inventory code or\n47|   table. Verified: separate derivation functions per package\n48|   (`deriveRefusalArms` vs `auditRefusalInventory`/`deriveRefusalInventory`\n49|   vs the terminalbackend file); the only cross-package touch is\n50|   `provider.Builtins()` IDs in a profile-mapping test, not inventory\n51|   machinery.\n52|3. Ownership figures reconciled against the pin test, NOT concatenated:\n53|   `TestREADMEOwnershipFiguresAreDerivedFromTheMeasuredReport` measures the\n54|   CURRENT tree (78 cases / 53 bindings in `ownership.v0.5.0.json`), so the\n55|   merged paragraph keeps 78 / 53. Writing 77 (trunk's number) or 81 would\n56|   redden the suite with no Go change allowed to fix it. Coverage block and\n57|   \"Fifty-three … 17/428\" kept (sibling untouched; pinned by\n58|   `tracecheck/main_test.go`).\n59|4. POST-INTEGRATION NOTE (for the integration run, not this CR): trunk JSON\n60|   holds 74 + 3 sibling cases (`terminal-manifest-probe-admission`,\n61|   `terminal-provider-descriptor-7a`, `terminal-lifecycle-conformance`);\n62|   this tree holds 74 + 4 ours (`provider-discovery-and-trust`,\n63|   `provhost-quiesce-proof`, `provhost-profile-mapping`,\n64|   `provhost-capability-gate`). Names are disjoint, so the union is 81\n65|   cases / 53 bindings — whoever resolves the `ownership.v0.5.0.json`\n66|   overlap at integrate time MUST also lift the README figures 78 → 81\n67|   (and re-pin), or the pin test goes red on trunk. Section bindings stay\n68|   53 (sibling added none).\n69|\n70|## Verification (this tree, after merge)\n71|\n72|- `go build ./...` → exit 0\n73|- `go test ./... -count=1` → exit 0, all 15 packages ok\n74|- `go vet ./...` → exit 0; gofmt gate clean\n75|- `TestREADMEOwnershipFiguresAreDerivedFromTheMeasuredReport` → PASS\n76|  (would FAIL on 77 or 81 — the concatenation defect, avoided)\n77|- `traceability/...`, `cliresult` GuardInventory, canonicaljson session\n78|  grammar README test → ok\n79|- Full-tree sha256 before/after: EXACTLY two paths differ — `LOGBOOK.md`,\n80|  `README.md`. Zero Go files (or any other file) changed.\n81|\n82|## Publication\n83|\n84|- Files differing from accepted rev 7: `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, nothing\n85|  else. Proven by full-tree sha256 before/after (no files added/removed,\n86|  only those two modified) plus rev-7-patch/worktree file-set identity.\n87|- Resulting revision: not yet published at handoff time. There is no\n88|  producer-side publish command by design — `Publish` runs in the\n89|  completion-time finalizer (`spawnruntime/changerequest.go`, gated on\n90|  `producerCompletionHandedOff`, which this handoff to `to-review`\n91|  satisfies). When this run finalizes, the publisher snapshots the tree\n92|  above into the next revision (expected: rev 8, `repository_delta`\n93|  present, same 60-path scope — file set unchanged, only the two files'\n94|  bytes moved) and runs the §6.2.1 validation suite against it with a\n95|  tree-drift check. Read the number back with\n96|  `task-board worktree status` (change-req line for TASK-260830-32jeti).\n97|- The combination still needs its review pass: the gate's complaint stands\n98|  until a reviewer looks at the two sides together (round-10 review of the\n99|  republished revision, then `accept_cr`, then integrate)."}}}
