{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c889","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07310-6156-7c60-80e0-f470e765d1c6"},"sequence":671,"recorded_at":1780531400001337,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7ae619ac-77e9-4550-bdb7-35ab99596fc0"},"task_id":"7ae619ac-77e9-4550-bdb7-35ab99596fc0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7ae619ac-77e9-4550-bdb7-35ab99596fc0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-35-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n '^## \\\\|^### ' /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree/LOGBOOK.md | head -40\",\n  \"description\": \"List merged LOGBOOK headers in order\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"6:## 2026-09-05\\n8:### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\\n25:### 0429 — Provider JSONL host leaf: protocol transport, three inherited findings, one repeated harness failure\\n37:### 0327 — The fourth enumeration failure: the refusal inventory could derive nothing and pass\\n47:## 2026-09-04\\n49:### 0230 — The guard the round did not sweep was the one that matters: uid 0 admitted, suite green\\n59:### 0210 — The inventory gate proves a site was reached, not that a test can tell which site fired\\n70:### 0115 — Provider discovery leaf: the inventory gate caught a test proving nothing, and a trust test caught a double hash\\n80:## 2026-09-03\\n82:### 1632 — The generalisation was written down one round earlier and still not executed: a list is a forced traversal, prose is a memory\\n97:### 1447 — The exit status a document declares is a member, not a fact: a guard proven on one code let a relabelled envelope forge a retry claim\\n112:### 1421 — A guard proven at one ordered pair admits a forged authority document, and the same blind spot sits in the sibling reader\\n126:### 1338 — A figure published beside a measurement must be derived from it, not restated next to it: third instance in one artifact\\n142:### 1231 — A gate proven at one sample is a gate proven at one sample: both §14.2 outcome guards shipped with a narrowing the suite could not see\\n157:### 1157 — Two conforming readers, one document: a repeated member is not a parse curiosity, it is a forged retry claim from a remote peer\\n175:### 1003 — An exit status is a class, not an identity: the fan-in is 47 codes over 17 statuses, and no CLI process exists to produce either\\n194:### 1015 — encoding/json is not a validator: it substitutes U+FFFD for a byte the contract requires to be valid UTF-8\\n210:### 0753 — Validate-then-alias is a bypass path, not a gate; and a clause claimed against the wrong actor\\n224:### 0742 — A key-name blacklist, again: the same shape BUG-260902-2faftr removed, caught by reading the logbook rather than by a test\\n239:### 0626 — Third instance of one class in one comment: the pin proved the digit and never the noun\\n253:### 0559 — The fix for a false claim shipped a false citation, and the bound that let it through said \\\"unmeasurable\\\" where the package already measured\\n265:### 0553 — A doc comment that promises a refusal is only pinnable if the doc is the test's input\\n278:### 0412 — Symbol reachability is not semantic coverage, and 48 bindings measured 2/394\\n292:### 0900 — \\\"No RFC 2119 keyword\\\" is a failure to measure, not an absence of obligation\\n304:### 0210 — A derived call graph that only sees `f(x)` covers 3 of 7 guards and looks complete\\n315:### 0135 — The fidelity fix reproduced its own bug, one schema over\\n326:### 0050 — Correcting one gate's input silently narrowed another gate\\n344:### 0035 — Stale line numbers turned a four-site audit into an eight-site class\\n358:### 0022 — The enumeration proved it agreed with itself, and nothing else\\n373:## 2026-09-02\\n375:### 2322 — One regex, two schemas, two opposite right answers\\n387:### 2237 — A fault suite that only proves the call failed proves the cheap half\\n399:### 2204 — A write that did not finish is not a mismatch either, and it was being quarantined as one\\n415:### 2122 — A byte bound measured on Go's escaped encoding is a bound nobody declared\\n427:### 2030 — A read that did not finish is not a mismatch, and quarantine cannot tell the difference on its own\\n439:### 1950 — Two Stories independently implemented the same normative section, and the registry only has room for one\\n450:### 1900 — An absent clause has nothing to mutate, and the artifact row read as if it were there\\n462:### 1810 — Two derived counts collided in one merge, and only one of them was honest\\n472:### 2240 — A pinned vocabulary set does not pin the JSON path that reaches it\\n483:### 2235 — Absence and grammar are different clauses, and requireExactMembers eats the first one\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4056,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1014,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
