{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07310-6156-7c60-80e0-f470e765d1c6"},"sequence":707,"recorded_at":1780531400001409,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"5b71b7a9-4dc6-4b7e-978c-55a525805305"},"task_id":"5b71b7a9-4dc6-4b7e-978c-55a525805305","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"5b71b7a9-4dc6-4b7e-978c-55a525805305","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-37-1\",\n  \"command\": \"W=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree/LOGBOOK.md; grep -c '0022' \\\"$W\\\"; grep -n '0022' \\\"$W\\\" | head; echo ===; grep -n '0935' /tmp/rev7recon/LOGBOOK.md | head -3; grep -n '0935' \\\"$W\\\" | head -3; echo ===; head -8 /tmp/trunk-added.txt\",\n  \"description\": \"Directly grep for sibling and our markers\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"8\\n318:- FINDING: three of the seven were regressions introduced by 0022. The pre-change cells said `exact git_index`, `uint32`, and `git-oid; matches object format` — accurate prose. The rewrite replaced them with verbatim quotes of a different schema. Same failure class the Bug exists to remove, produced by the fix.\\n321:- FINDING: the blank-line block separator from 0022 did not stop a quote crossing the newline between two adjacent table rows, which is not a blank line. `Lease Record.holder_host_id` quoting its own row stitched to the `predecessor_lease_id` row after it was admitted by the whole package. A table row is a complete line by construction, so no honest excerpt spans two; the newline between two table lines is now a hard boundary too. The `README.md` and artifact claim that whitespace collapsing forgave hard wrapping and table indentation \\\"and nothing else\\\" was false in both files and is now stated as what it is.\\n328:- ROOT CAUSE: `sessionRecordGrammarFamily` classified a constraint enumeration row into an executable grammar family by substring-matching the row's `Pinned SPEC declaration` prose. That column is the fidelity artifact 0022 rewrote. Replacing informative-but-partly-fabricated prose with verbatim `SPEC.md` fragments removed the words the classifier greps for, so eight rows fell out of `TestSessionRecordDeclaredGrammarRowsReachIdentityProductionEntries` and stopped being attacked with invalid grammar values through both public identity entries. Measured on both trees with the same command: 18 rows -> 11, 107 subtests -> 66, `reverse-dns` 11 -> 4.\\n329:- FINDING: the completeness check was `familyCounts[family] == 0`. Four is not zero, so a 64% narrowing of the largest family reported nothing. A non-empty guard on a derived set is the same defect class as the non-empty guard on the excerpt column that 0022 exists to remove — one level up, in the gate doing the removing.\\n337:- FINDING: the excerpt gate was shape-blind. Retargeting `ManifestEntry.file.size` from `:4746` to BlobChunk's bounded `:4622` clause — a different schema, a bound that member does not carry — left the whole package green. Same cross-schema class as the `environment_id` finding in 0022, which was found by reading the document, not by the gate.\\n358:### 0022 — The enumeration proved it agreed with itself, and nothing else\\n535:- DECISION: `endpoint = \\\"peer.example:022\\\"` is admitted; a leading-zero port reads as decimal 22 and carries no option or whitespace. Review flagged that the case named `padded port` pinned only the 1..5-byte length bound, so the name overclaimed. `:022` is now pinned as admitted reviewed behaviour, and the length bound gets cases that rest on it alone (`:000022` and `:0000022`, decimal 22 and inside the numeric bound, so only `len(port) > 5` refuses them).\\n538:- REGRESSION: rev2 review found one live surviving mutant, and it was introduced by the previous cycle: narrowing `admitEndpointPort` from `len(port) > 5` to `> 6` kept the whole suite green while admitting `peer.example:000022`. The case that owned the clause, `port over length bound`, uses a *seven*-byte port, which stays refused under the narrowed bound — so it pinned the bound to somewhere in [5,6] rather than to 5. The reviewed baseline patch of BUG-260902-3c7ovg had a six-byte `padded port` case that killed this mutant exactly, and rev2 replaced it. The earlier claim that both surviving mutants were equivalent was true of the 28 mutants that cycle ran, but that set contained only the *deletion* of this bound, never its one-step narrowing, and the entry above is corrected to say so. No exposure: the strings newly admitted are six-byte zero-padded ports whose decimal value is already inside 1..65535 and which `ssh(1)` resolves identically. The defect was in the evidence, not the gate.\\n===\\n8:### 0935 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: switch vocabularies, ExecRunner frame loss, flake bound\\n===\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0022 — Leaf-2 round-1 rework: refusal arms that share one code need clause assertions, not code assertions\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 rework after CHANGES REQUESTED (F1–F5, F9, G-A blocking; F6–F8 non-blocking). Production: `CheckOperation` admits `manifest`/`probe` with no capability dependency (§4.D); dead probe-identity branch and subsumed platform-dup check removed; `checkEvidenceSet` doc corrected to whole-reconciliation refusal. Tests: every refusal assertion in `manifest_test.go`/`manifest_pin_test.go` now names `*Error.Detail` (was 0/29); four over-determined `TestReconcileRefusals` fixtures narrowed until only the named rule rejects; `ParseProbe`/`ParseEvidence` gain the schema/version/identity/kind/digest cases only `ParseManifest` had; `now == expires_at` boundary row added.\\n- STRUCTURAL ROOT: ~110 of 121 arms return `CodeMismatch`, so deleting a gate slides its fixture onto a lower arm and a code-only suite stays green. Against the narrowed fixtures all six re-runs (4 arm-shift gates + record-digest + expiry-boundary) fail with `error = <nil>`: the deleted gate admits what it must reject, and no lower arm catches the fixture.\\n- F1 (live spec violation): `CheckOperation(\\\"manifest\\\"|\\\"probe\\\")` refused `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` even fully admitted; §4.D gives both `Capability dependencies: none` and neither row allows that code. Pinned by `TestCheckOperationAdmitsDependencyFreeOperations` (empty + full admitted sets, plus the still-refused gated operation).\\n- F3 NARROWING SHAPE: the AdmitProbe substitution fixture now tracks the foreign digest in the probe, so probe↔manifest identity holds and only the manifest↔record gate can refuse. Same-shape-different-arm cases are indistinguishable by any assertion when both arms share code AND detail — the fixture, not the assertion, must isolate the arm.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5849,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1463,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
