{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c961","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07310-6156-7c60-80e0-f470e765d1c6"},"sequence":779,"recorded_at":1780531400001553,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3fe00ee8-abdc-4192-a61d-8ca7cf49da53"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e155541a-22ed-489c-8f60-a44bd5423fb5"},"task_id":"e155541a-22ed-489c-8f60-a44bd5423fb5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e155541a-22ed-489c-8f60-a44bd5423fb5","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-41-1\",\n  \"command\": \"W=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree; git -C \\\"$W\\\" status | head -30; echo ===; ls \\\"$W/.git/rebase-merge/\\\" 2>/dev/null | head; cat \\\"$W/.git/rebase-merge/done\\\" 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-32jeti/reapply.md 2>/dev/null | head -100\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect rebase state and reapply brief\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"On branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-3jqsx1\\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\\n===\\n===\\nThe Story branch has just been replayed onto the current trunk. Your job is to\\nrestore the accepted work onto that new base and republish — nothing else.\\n\\n## What happened, so you know why the worktree looks empty\\n\\nThe accepted Change Request revision 7 was built on a branch forked at\\n`57afcc6`. The sibling Story then landed, moving trunk to `2512f20`, and §6.2\\ncorrectly invalidated the acceptance because both Stories change `LOGBOOK.md`.\\n\\nA previous run merged that overlap well — both sides of `LOGBOOK.md` kept whole\\nwith zero lines dropped either way, and two real `README.md` resolutions rather\\nthan concatenation. But the branch itself still forked from the old trunk, so\\nChange Request construction failed with\\n`change_request_base_authority_mismatch`, and the board can only move a branch\\nwhose worktree is clean.\\n\\nSo the work was stashed to let the board replay the branch. It is not lost:\\n\\n- `git stash list` holds it as `stash@{0}`;\\n- a full archive is at\\n  `.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/backup/worktree-pre-refresh.tgz`;\\n- the merged documents are saved at\\n  `.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/backup/LOGBOOK.merged.md` and `README.merged.md`;\\n- the accepted candidate is recorded on the board as\\n  `TASK-260830-32jeti_change-request_rev7.patch`.\\n\\n## What to do\\n\\n1. Restore the stash onto the refreshed branch (`git stash pop`). If it\\n   conflicts, prefer the recorded artifacts: apply\\n   `TASK-260830-32jeti_change-request_rev7.patch` for the Go work, then copy the\\n   two saved merged documents into place.\\n2. Verify the restoration is complete and correct:\\n   - every Go file from revision 7 is present and byte-identical to the patch;\\n   - `LOGBOOK.md` keeps **both** Stories' entries, with the sibling's blocks\\n     byte-identical to trunk;\\n   - `README.md` carries the two resolutions the previous run made.\\n3. Run the suite green: `go test ./... -count=1`, `-race`, `vet`,\\n   `GOOS=windows go vet`, `gofmt`, and `tracecheck`.\\n4. Publish the Change Request.\\n\\n## Do not\\n\\n- Do not change any Go file. The accepted tree carries a full review round —\\n  177 mutant rows across sixteen batteries with zero resurrections — and any\\n  edit to production or test code invalidates all of it.\\n- Do not drop, reorder or rewrite the sibling Story's landed `LOGBOOK.md`\\n  entries.\\n- Do not commit by hand, do not touch `main`, do not push to any remote.\\n\\n## Report\\n\\nThe published revision, its `repository_delta`, and confirmation that the tree\\ndiffers from revision 7 in exactly `LOGBOOK.md` and `README.md` and nothing\\nelse. If anything else differs, stop and report it rather than proceeding.\\n\\nIf the branch was **not** replayed onto `2512f20` — check with\\n`git merge-base --is-ancestor 2512f20 HEAD` — stop and report that first,\\nbecause republishing on the old base would fail the same way again.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2904,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 726,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
