ty_mismatch`, and the board can only move a branch\\nwhose worktree is clean.\\n\\nSo the work was stashed to let the board replay the branch. It is not lost:\\n\\n- `git stash list` holds it as `stash@{0}`;\\n- a full archive is at\\n  `.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/backup/worktree-pre-refresh.tgz`;\\n- the merged documents are saved at\\n  `.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/backup/LOGBOOK.merged.md` and `README.merged.md`;\\n- the accepted candidate is recorded on the board as\\n  `TASK-260830-32jeti_change-request_rev7.patch`.\\n\\n## What to do\\n\\n1. Restore the stash onto the refreshed branch (`git stash pop`). If it\\n   conflicts, prefer the recorded artifacts: apply\\n   `TASK-260830-32jeti_change-request_rev7.patch` for the Go work, then copy the\\n   two saved merged documents into place.\\n2. Verify the restoration is complete and correct:\\n   - every Go file from revision 7 is present and byte-identical to the patch;\\n   - `LOGBOOK.md` keeps **both** Stories' entries, with the sibling's blocks\\n     byte-identical to trunk;\\n   - `README.md` carries the two resolutions the previous run made.\\n3. Run the suite green: `go test ./... -count=1`, `-race`, `vet`,\\n   `GOOS=windows go vet`, `gofmt`, and `tracecheck`.\\n4. Publish the Change Request.\\n\\n## Do not\\n\\n- Do not change any Go file. The accepted tree carries a full review round —\\n  177 mutant rows across sixteen batteries with zero resurrections — and any\\n  edit to production or test code invalidates all of it.\\n- Do not drop, reorder or rewrite the sibling Story's landed `LOGBOOK.md`\\n  entries.\\n- Do not commit by hand, do not touch `main`, do not push to any remote.\\n\\n## Report\\n\\nThe published revision, its `repository_delta`, and confirmation that the tree\\ndiffers from revision 7 in exactly `LOGBOOK.md` and `README.md` and nothing\\nelse. If anything else differs, stop and report it rather than proceeding.\\n\\nIf the branch was **not** replayed onto `2512f20` — check with\\n`git merge-base --is-ancestor 2512f20 HEAD` — stop and report that first,\\nbecause republishing on the old base would fail the same way again.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2904,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 726,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
